  "id": "Compound::DB05294 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Vandetanib may interact with Cyp3a4 through multiple pathways, primarily via its binding to the enzyme. Pathway 1 links Vandetanib to Nail Abnormality Nos, which is caused by Propafenone, and Propafenone binds to Cyp3a4. Pathway 2 connects Vandetanib to Peripheral Sensorimotor Neuropathy, caused by Disulfiram, which also binds to Cyp3a4. Pathway 3 links Vandetanib to Cardiac Failure Acute, caused by Maraviroc, which binds to Cyp3a4. These interactions indicate that Vandetanib may influence Cyp3a4 activity through the binding of different compounds, which in turn may modulate enzyme function. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions—Secondary Amino Compound, Organochalcogen Compound, and Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound—suggest a broader class of compounds that could mediate this relationship. The evidence supports a potential role for Vandetanib in modulating Cyp3a4 activity, though the exact mechanism and extent of this interaction require further investigation.",
